.TH SDL_ANALYZER_NORETURN 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ANALYZER_NORETURN \- A macro to tag a function as never-returning (for analysis purposes).
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_begin_code.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_ANALYZER_NORETURN __attribute__((analyzer_noreturn))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is almost identical to
.BR SDL_NORETURN ,
except functions marked with this _can_ actually return\[char46] The difference is that this isn\(aqt used for code generation, but rather static analyzers use this information to assume truths about program state and available code paths\[char46] Specifically, this tag is useful for writing an assertion mechanism\[char46] Indeed,
.BR SDL_assert
uses this tag behind the scenes\[char46] Generally, apps that don\(aqt understand the specific use-case for this tag should avoid using it directly\[char46]
.PP
On compilers without analyzer_noreturn support, this is defined to nothing\[char46]
.PP
This symbol is used in SDL\(aqs headers, but apps and other libraries are welcome to use it for their own interfaces as well\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

